/**
    Slant slider

    The Material effect with skewed panels. Written from scratch: no custom JS,
    no clip-path, and nothing that reaches into Material's own layout.

    ── Why skew and not clip-path ──
    skew() turns the box itself into a parallelogram, so two adjacent panels
    tile exactly — A's sheared right edge lands on B's sheared left edge, top
    and bottom, with no gap and nothing to reconcile. clip-path instead REMOVES
    material from a rectangle, so touching boxes can never have touching
    diagonals. That is why the clip-path version needed a JS module to overlap
    the panels, and why that module then had to be kept in step with Material
    frame by frame. Skew needs none of it.

    ── The bug the usual skew version has ──
    The panel skews one way and the image counter-skews the other. That only
    cancels if both share a transform origin AND the image is wide enough to
    cover the panel's sheared extent. skewX(a) about the centre pushes the top
    edge out by height * tan(a) / 2 one way and the bottom the same the other,
    so a panel spans height * tan(a) more than its box. Reference versions tend
    to hardcode that slack as a viewport multiple (170vw and the like) — a
    WIDTH, while the shear it must cover derives from the HEIGHT. So it holds on
    wide screens and opens a triangular gap in a top corner on narrow ones.
    Deriving the slack from the height is the whole fix, and it is exact at
    every size.

    ── What Material still owns ──
    The wrapper's width and transform, which is the smooth expand. Nothing here
    touches either: the skew goes on the slide and the counter-skew on the
    media, both of which Material leaves alone.
*/

.slider-slants{
    --slant-angle: 10deg;
    --slant-height: clamp(380px, 56vh, 620px);

    /* Total horizontal spread skewX(--slant-angle) adds across the full height,
       half above the centre line and half below. The media must be exactly this
       much wider than its panel to cover it. */
    --slant-shear: calc(var(--slant-height) * tan(var(--slant-angle)));

    --swiper-material-slide-border-radius: 0;

    position: relative;

    &__int{
        position: relative;
        height: var(--slant-height);
        /* Sheared edges reach half the shear past the panel box; bleed by that
           so the outermost panels meet the viewport instead of stopping short. */
        margin-inline: calc(var(--slant-shear) * -0.5);
    }

    &__container{
        display: block;
        height: var(--slant-height);
    }

    /* The slant. On the slide, not the wrapper — Material rewrites the
       wrapper's transform every frame and would overwrite this. */
    &__slide{
        transform: skewX(calc(var(--slant-angle) * -1));
    }

    &__content{
        position: relative;
        height: 100%;
        background-color: var(--gray-light);
    }

    /* Undoes the slide's skew so the photo is never distorted, widened by
       exactly the shear so it still covers the parallelogram top and bottom.
       Same transform origin as the slide (both default to centre), so the two
       cancel precisely — which is what the reference gets wrong. */
    &__media{
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        left: calc(var(--slant-shear) * -0.5);
        width: calc(100% + var(--slant-shear));
        transform: skewX(var(--slant-angle));

        img,
        picture{
            display: block;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            object-fit: cover;
        }
    }

    /* Counter-skewed too, or the text leans. */
    &__info{
        position: absolute;
        z-index: var(--z-raised);
        inset-inline: 0;
        bottom: 0;

        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: var(--spacer-2);

        padding: var(--spacer-6) var(--spacer-5) var(--spacer-5);
        padding-inline-start: calc(var(--spacer-5) + var(--slant-shear));

        color: var(--text-color-light);
        background: linear-gradient(to top, rgb(0 0 0 / 72%), transparent);
        transform: skewX(var(--slant-angle));
    }

    &__heading,
    &__preheading{
        color: inherit;
        text-wrap: balance;
    }

    &__intro{
        color: inherit;
        max-width: 46ch;
    }

    .swiper-actions{
        position: absolute;
        z-index: var(--z-raised);
        right: var(--spacer-4);
        bottom: var(--spacer-4);

        display: flex;
        gap: var(--spacer-2);
    }
}
